# VS Code Extension Tests

Apply when editing integration tests under `src/test/` (or path in stack.md `test_roots`). Subagent: `vscode-extension-agent` or `test-agent`.

## Layout

- `src/test/runTest.ts` — `@vscode/test-electron` entry
- `src/test/suite/*.test.ts` — Mocha test suites
- `src/test/suite/index.ts` — test runner
- `test-fixtures/` — committed sample files

Adjust paths if stack.md defines different `test_roots`.

## Conventions

- Test names describe **What** (expected outcome), include TC ID when from testspec
- Pattern: `'TC-010: format command updates document'`
- Use `vscode.commands.executeCommand` for command scenarios
- Avoid fixed `setTimeout` — use condition-based `waitFor`
- Restore configuration and workspace state in `finally` blocks
- Do not depend on network or Marketplace in tests

## Isolation

- Prefer `launchArgs: ['--disable-extensions']` in runTest.ts
- Each test must be runnable independently where possible

## Before finishing

Run `test_single` or `test_all` from [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md).
